From tru64-unix-managers  Fri Oct 27 18:20:57 1995
From: Scott Chapman <chapman () atria ! com>
Date: Fri, 27 Oct 1995 18:20:57 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Screen resolutions
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96075324106802

Hi,
Thanks to the many people who sent me email. I have fixed the problem...

The  issue is that you must specify the screen resolution to the Xserver. This
is done by editing the Xserver file in /var/X11/xdm (or in the /usr/dt/config
directory if you are running CDE).

You need to add "-screen:0 <resolution>" to the end of the line beginning with
":0", where resolution is one of (640, 800, 1024, 1280) or whatever resolutions
your graphics card supports. You can find out what your card supports by
checking your hardware documentation...

Scott.

