From tru64-unix-managers  Thu Oct 26 17:41:30 1995
From: risler () cgm ! cnrs-gif ! fr
Date: Thu, 26 Oct 1995 17:41:30 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: [SUMMARY] Registering OSF-USR
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96075324106768

Dear all,

You are just great, I've received 23 answers so far!! They all give the 
same solution for registering the unlimited OSF license:

1) Normal way

# lmf delete osf-usr   ! this will delete the default 2 users pack
# lmf register - < osf-usr  ! assuming you are on the CD in the right 
				directory (packs-unix or something like 
				that)
# lmf load 0 osf-usr
# lmf reset


2) If you have loaded the unlimited license without deleting the default 
   you must delete the default because it takes precedence over the unlimited 
   pack. It is not necessary to delete and re-load the unlimited pack.

# lmf list full for osf-usr
	you'll see 2 entries. The default 2 users entry that you want to 
	delete is called OSF-BASE-IMPLICIT-USER
# lmf delete osf-usr DEC OSF-BASE-IMPLICIT-USER
# lmf reset

The last command now makes the unlimited license active.

Check with # lmf list

and you'll see

OSF-USR		active		unlimited

My deepest thanks to:

