From tru64-unix-managers  Wed Oct 25 18:38:08 1995
From: risler () cgm ! cnrs-gif ! fr
Date: Wed, 25 Oct 1995 18:38:08 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: [SUMMARY] Printing on a remote DecLaser 3500
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96075324106746

Hi,

I had problems printing on a DecLaser 3500 through IP (didn't print 
anything).

The answer came from Rene Laudert and Lucien Hercaud: this printer does 
speak TCP/IP but doesn't speak lpd !!
When setting up the printer with the software provided with it, a daemon is 
discreetly launched -which is totally undocumented in my doc. If, for one 
reason or another, you reboot your machine -which I did- the daemon is lost 
... and the printer also. 
So, in order to print, you must type (or add in rc3.d, of course):

/usr/nic/nic_print /dev/nic/my_printer my_printer 10001 [&]

which is not totally obvious....

The software also creates a printcap entry which works OK.

Well, now that it works, I find the 3500 a very good machine. Excellent 
also for my PC.

My thanks also to:

J. Buchanan, K. Hellebo, R. Muse and D.R. Courtade

Jean-Loup

