 Dear Managers,

 The information in my original post was correct. For correct changes from
 BST to GST for the United Kingdom and Ireland modify 
 /etc/zoneinfo/sources/europe and change

 # Current rules
 Rule    GB-Eire 1981    max     -       Mar     lastSun 1:00s   1:00    BST
 Rule    GB-Eire 1972    max     -       Oct     Sun>=23 1:00s   0       GMT

 to

 Rule    GB-Eire 1996    max     -       Mar     lastSun   1:00s   1:00    BST
 Rule    GB-Eire 1995    only    -       Oct     22        1:00s   0       GMT
 Rule    GB-Eire 1996    max     -       Oct     lastSun   1:00s   0       GMT

 or something similar, then update using zic, e.g.

 # zic -l GB-Eire /etc/zoneinfo/sources/europe

 This can be checked with zdump

 # zdump -v GB-Eire

 This also works for DECstations running Ultrix, and all my hosts showed the
 correct time when I got to work this morning.  This will all be corrected 
 in future releases of Digital Unix.

 The fix can be applied retroactively, but your clocks will change right away. 
  
 Ray Bellis pointed out that you don't have to worry about changing all your
 NFS hosts timezones as dates are stored in UTC. 
 
