To recap:
>I've just upgraded an Alpha with a local printer from 1.3a to 3.0, (3.2c 
>another day!), and now all the other Alphas in my department (already at
>3.0) can no longer print to it.

And the solution was to make sure the names of the Alphas wanting to 
print on the local printer are in the /etc/hosts.lpd file of the machine 
with the local printer. For some reason an empty /etc/hosts.lpd worked fine 
under 1.3a, but 3.0 is much more strict.

Thank you one and all!

Chris Stoddart 
Dept. of Physics
The Open University

