Hi all,

Since my last posting I have received some more replies which contain 
useful information beyond that in the first one.

To recap, the question related to support of the DE500-XA ethernet 
interface on the ALPHAstation 200 4/100. The original summary reported 
that it was, in V3.2C.

Dr. Tom Blinn <tpb@zk3.dec.com> confirmed that the DE500-XA was supported
under Digital UNIX V3.2C but queried whether it had been "qualified" on
the 200 4/100 and suggested I check the SPD. I have now done that and can
confirm that it is. 

Herve DEMARTHE (CEA France) <demarthe@alpha.cad.cea.fr> reported that a
patch might be required. Rajul Shah USG <rajul@zk3.dec.com> confirmed that
a fix/patch was required if the DE500 was used on a fairly loaded system.
He stated that this would be available from support within a few weeks. He 
also gave the following information on configuring the interface: 

   In the absence of console firmware support (for either booting or
   setting the 10 or 100 speeds), one can use the ifconfig command to
   configure the interface like so:

   # ifconfig tu0 speed 10              ; selects 10 speed half-duplex
   # ifconfig tu0 speed 20              ; selects 10 speed full-duplex
   # ifconfig tu0 speed 100             ; selects 100 speed half-duplex
   # ifconfig tu0 speed 200             ; selects 100 speed full-duplex

   Alternatively, you can simply do the above during IP configuration
   in your /etc/rc.config file. For example:

   IFCONFIG_0="a.b.c.d netmask 255.255.255.0 speed 100"

Harald Lundberg <hl@tekla.fi> stated that he had also asked the 
question and was told that V3.2C and firmware rev 4.2 were required.

Selden E Ball Jr <SEB@LNS62.LNS.CORNELL.EDU> reported that they were
running DE500's in two AlphaStation 200 4/166 systems under V3.2C. 

Thanks also to Helgi Viggosson <helgi@ott.is> and any others who have 
replied who I may have missed.

The moral of this story is : "Wait before summarising!"

