Subject: SUMMARY: Netscape 1.12 dumps core under OSF/1 on AXP
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96075324106549

Barely twenty minutes after posting my query, I got a reply, including
a correct diagnosis.  Many thanks to timothy@persimmon.com, who wrote:

|   Just a thought, but I've seen a similar problem on Linux which was
| caused by the presence of the old preferences files, cache, etc. If
| you do an 'ls -a' and then mv away anything that looks like it came
| from 'netscape' (or 'mozilla' for that matter), it might work.

Sure enough, simply doing a "rm -rf .MCOM-*" in my home directory caused
netscape 1.12 to work fine.  (It names its files ".netscape-*", but does
seem to get confused by the existence of old ".MCOM-*" files.)  Loads of
thanks to Timothy, and thanks in advance to everyone else who's already
sent suggestions which haven't arrived yet!

